\section{Why this one needs no account}{

MUR and the VIIRS products are also at PO.DAAC, where they need an Earthdata
login. ERDDAP serves them openly and subsets server-side, so a bounding box
costs a small download rather than a global file. That is the whole reason
this route was chosen: no credentials for this package to handle, and none
for you to configure.
}

\section{Satellite SST is not model SST}{

\code{MUR} measures the \strong{foundation} temperature — below the daily warming layer
— where a model's \code{SST} is its topmost level, and satellite chlorophyll is an
optical retrieval where a model's is a state variable. Both land in columns
called \code{SST} and \code{CHL}, which is what makes them drop into an existing
pipeline, and is exactly why \code{\link[=matchData]{matchData()}} records \verb{<var>_source}.

Two further cautions specific to satellites. \strong{MUR is gap-free by
construction} — it is an analysis, so cloud is interpolated over rather than
left as \code{NA}, and \code{SST_ERROR} is where the uncertainty of that shows up; fetch
it alongside if the interpolation matters. And \strong{\code{VIIRSCHL} is DINEOF
gap-filled}, so its holes are filled too; \code{VIIRSCHL2018} is the raw
retrieval and is gappy under cloud, which \code{\link[=fill_satellite_gaps]{fill_satellite_gaps()}} is for.
}

